      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Bombieri argues that zeta is a prototype and that functional equations and Euler products often come from modular parametrization or simultaneous Laplacian-Hecke eigenstructure, with establishing those sources already difficult; the Selberg class abstracts the shared analytic package and primitive factorization, but leaves the tasks of proving its members arithmetic and proving prime-coefficient orthogonality or a prime number theorem.",
