    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b18a19b72daa208501fc23eb9df52c83ceab869d18478ff6aebc4a038d74d119",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Semi-local scaling operators canonically reproduce finite local terms of the explicit formula, but the proposed Hardy-space proof fails because local-factor ratios can have unit modulus on the critical line without being bounded, and the resulting sign inequality is false; the authors identify the omitted global Poisson normalization as essential, in contrast with the finite-field setting where an intersection theorem forces the sign.",
