    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_bfb105f3d18275277bddb809325f8da451a7d38b1531e9a567072d525bb00629",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Riemann's prime-counting formula already required the zero terms to be ordered by magnitude because rearrangement can change the value; the later Delsarte-Weil formulation relocates the same prime-zero duality into a distribution evaluated on test functions, where the summation convention, contour decay, and admissible function class become explicit parts of the interface.",
