      "proposed_content": "The 1990 certificate searched for a nonreal zero of a Jensen polynomial for a chosen heat parameter, but its required degree and precision exploded as the parameter approached zero; the 1993 Lehmer-pair certificate instead used a consecutive pair of zeros of H0 whose squared gap is small relative to a rigorously bounded inverse-square interaction with all other zeros.",
