      "proposed_content": "Voronin universality approximates nonvanishing holomorphic targets on compact subsets of 1/2 < Re(s) < 1 by vertical zeta shifts, while Borchsenius-Jessen shows that every nonzero value x is assumed infinitely often arbitrarily close to the critical line from the right; together they isolate zero alignment as a property not preserved by generic value-distribution flexibility.",
